            "The categories move over time. An assumption that proves false often becomes an issue; a dependency on another team becomes a schedule constraint once its date is fixed. Keep assumptions, issues and dependencies in a [RAID log](/project-management/raid-log/) and keep constraints in the charter and scope statement, where they are visible to the people who approve the plan. Treat any assumption that underpins a constraint, such as \"the budget will be released in April\", as a candidate risk for the [project risk](/project-management/project-risk/) register.",
